title lotus-audio — Lotus's stereo reverb tone, the axis whole
prompt recur loop — continue the Lotus/lotus-audio ladder the Long Return Lila, each finished rung its own signed round
think lotus-audio gave the mono reverb its darkness knob (a high-cut on the reverberant tail); the ladder always closes the mono/stereo pair, so the thin twin is stereo_reverb_tone — the same high-cut over both channels of a StereoClip, one shared coefficient, the image held. Mirrored the stereo_reverb_predelay (lotus-audio) shape exactly.
think Reverberate the master wet through lotus-audio stereo_reverb_preset unchanged, precheck the tone coefficient through lotus-audio tone.precheck BEFORE the wet is written (atomicity — a bad tone leaves both channels dry and balanced), then low_pass each channel with the same coefficient, no cross-channel read so the image is held. StereoReverbToneError = stereo_reverb_preset.StereoReverbPresetError || BadTone.
obs Witness GREEN on the first metal pass — no RED to book. Six laws: the identity edge on both channels, each channel equals its composition byte for byte, each channel darkens (roughness strictly reduced), the image held (centred identical, stereo distinct), channels balanced + silence, faults forward atomic (BadTone both channels dry, DurationTooLong, BadRange). lotus-audio stereo preset and lotus-audio mono tone re-run GREEN beside it; TAME bans clean, width exit 0.
loom witness=ales_stereo_reverb_tone_witness selftest=GREEN laws=6 channels=2 max_clip=4096 bench_samples=1024
file active-designing/20260815-104900_fill-ales199-lotus-stereo-reverb-tone.md the self-approved design round naming the crux, shape, and six laws
file lotus/stereo_reverb_tone.rye the rung — the stereo wet-tail darkness knob, lotus-audio low-pass per ear over lotus-audio wet, prechecked
file tools/ales_stereo_reverb_tone_witness.rish the witness proving six laws and re-proving lotus-audio/lotus-audio green beside it
recommend keep-going — the tone axis stands whole for mono and stereo; the richer horizon is a true in-loop damped-comb primitive (a low-pass inside each comb's feedback so later echoes darken progressively), or a fresh reverb axis (width, freeze, early/late balance).
